# Keep the workshop off the public server.
#
# design-lab/ is where the redesign is made: prototypes, working notes, the
# design brief and constitution, hero caption ledgers, and ~850MB of master
# artwork. None of it is linked from the site, but anything uploaded to the
# host is fetchable by anyone who knows the address — "not linked" is not
# "not published".
#
# The two pages that ARE public were promoted out of it and now live at the
# site root: welcome.html (the front door) and teach.html, together with the
# 58 assets they actually request (3.3MB) under assets/. Nothing left in
# design-lab/ is needed to serve them — verified by recording every request
# the pages make at desktop and phone widths.
design-lab/

# Python content pipeline — server-side tooling, never served to a browser.
# Verified: no api/ function and no client-side fetch reads from it.
scripts/

# Local scratch
scratchpad/

# NOT excluded, deliberately:
#   specs/  — admin/build-status.html fetches /specs/index.json at runtime.
#   data/   — js/exam-countdown.js fetches /data/exam-dates-*.json.
# Both are read by the live site. Excluding either breaks a working page.
